The original poster (Michal) didn't mean to say that you cannot get an
AC of lower than -18 (I believe, b.t.w., that the real number is -10),
but that you don't get any more benefits of an AC lower than the number
mentioned. When your AC drops below -10, your chance of being hit does
not change any more. The only (slight) advantage, I believe, is that
when you DO get hit, you receive less damage. It might still influence
the chance of being hit by a ray or something like that, I'm not sure
about that.

